  "question": {
    "text": "The electric field in a region is given by $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{E}}=(2 \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+4 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}+6 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}}) \\times 10^3 \\mathrm{~N} / \\mathrm{C}$. The flux of the field through a rectangular surface parallel to $x-z$ plane is $6.0 \\mathrm{Nm}^2 \\mathrm{C}^{-1}$. The area of the surface is ________ $\\mathrm{cm}^2$."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "15",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\phi=\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{E}} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{A}}=(2 \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+4 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}+6 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}}) \\times 10^3 \\cdot \\mathrm{~A} \\hat{\\mathrm{j}} \\\\ & 6=4 \\times 10^3 \\mathrm{~A} \\\\ & \\mathrm{~A}=1.5 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~m}^2 \\\\ & =15 \\mathrm{~cm}^2\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}